# Docker matches these from the build-context root, so a bare name (e.g. "node_modules")
# only excludes the top-level entry. "**/" matches zero or more directories, so each
# "**/name" pattern below excludes that name at any depth. The Dockerfiles run their own
# `pnpm install` / build steps, so none of these host-side artifacts are needed.

# Dependencies and build output
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.turbo
**/.venv
**/__pycache__

# Env files at any depth: ".env*" covers .env, .env.prod, .env.local, etc. A bare ".env"
# used to let apps/backend/.env into the published backend image.
**/.env*
# ...except the committed template, which holds no secrets.
!**/.env.example

# Local tooling and editor state (Claude worktrees alone are gigabytes)
.git
.claude
.mcp.json
**/.idea
**/.DS_Store

# Private notes that are gitignored but would still be copied from a working checkout
CLAUDE.md
collections-plan.md
relaunch-plan.md
